# B&G (mfg 381, src 28, Navigation Management) PGN 129285 with Latin-1 text in
# STRING_LAU control byte 1 — captured 2026-08-29. Evidence for canboat#864.
#
# Route name  0d 01 46 e6 6b 65 20 72 6f 75 74 e9 00
#             len 13 = 2 header + 10 chars + NUL (the terminator IS counted)
#             control 1, then Latin-1: 46 "F", e6 "æ", ... e9 "é"  = "Fæke routé"
#             e6 is not valid UTF-8, so this cannot be read as UTF-8.
#
# Waypoint 2  4d 61 74 73 3f 72 61 20 53 65   = "Mats?ra Se"
#             The name was typed with a character outside Latin-1 (U+016B "ū").
#             The plotter itself substituted an ASCII '?' before transmitting —
#             i.e. this device cannot put non-Latin-1 text on the bus at all.
#
# Today canboat C emits the e6/e9 bytes raw (making the JSON line invalid UTF-8)
# and canboat Rust / keel emit U+FFFD (destroying the byte value).
